From 1f1ae5cc394194aa46053c3fdad3845592e13676 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 07:52:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 84/90] phy: rockchip-inno-usb2: Power the PHY up before the
 host starts

Switching to host mode only queued the OTG state machine, so the PHY was
powered up whenever that work happened to run. dwc3 sets the PHY mode
and then immediately starts the host controller, which put the power up
in the middle of the xHCI probe:

  8.009  U2PHY set_mode: host=1
  8.011  xhci-hcd: xHCI Host Controller
  8.044  xhci-hcd: new USB bus registered, assigned bus number 8
  8.054  U2PHY power_on
  8.066  xhci-hcd: new USB bus registered, assigned bus number 9

A device that is already attached has to be visible by the time the root
hub is registered, and here it was not: an attached storage dongle never
enumerated at all. It used to work by accident, because the mode was set
after the host was up and the power up landed after the whole probe.

Take the host transition immediately instead. Device mode still goes
through the state machine, which has to work out what the port is facing
before it can do anything anyway.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
index 96d0042027a4..ffbe80342189 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -731,7 +731,20 @@ static int rockchip_usb2phy_set_mode(struct phy *phy, enum phy_mode mode,
 	 */
 	rockchip_chg_detect_cancel(rphy, rport);
 
-	/* let the state machine act on the new role */
+	if (host_mode) {
+		/*
+		 * The controller starts the host right after this returns, and
+		 * the device is already attached, so its connect has to be
+		 * visible by then. Leaving the power up to the state machine
+		 * lands it somewhere in the middle of the host controller
+		 * probe, and the connect is missed.
+		 */
+		rport->state = OTG_STATE_A_HOST;
+		rockchip_usb2phy_power_on(phy);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	/* let the state machine work out what a device mode port is facing */
 	mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &rport->otg_sm_work, 0);
 
 	return 0;
